# (#126) A MODULE-scope for binder in an OBSERVED program, un-named.
#
# This arm is deliberately NOT per-name and the fixture is what pins that.
# The module binder is renamed to a fresh env slot in every observed
# program, because module-scope for-UNBOXING is still gated on the
# whole-program flag: an un-named binder there is STILL env-resident, so
# skipping the rename would leak the same phantom post-loop binding the
# round-65 rename exists to prevent. The fresh name is in no census, so
# every arm below treats it as the env-resident binder it is.
ch is 1.0
acc is 0.0
for v in [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]:
    acc is acc + v
    ch is ch * 0.5
print of f"acc {acc} ch {ch}"
print of f"ch-report {report of ch}"
